  "notes": "Enter age as the first line (subtract 10 for women), then add the rest. PSI can under-triage young patients with few comorbidities but significant physiologic derangement — always overlay clinical judgement, hypoxaemia, ability to take oral meds, and social factors. CURB-65 is the quicker bedside alternative (no labs). Neither score decides ICU admission — that is the ATS/IDSA criteria.",
  "buildNote": "Additive; total = age (−10 if female) + weighted points. Five risk classes."
